# Every variable this service reads is declared in src/env.ts and appears here; nothing else is
# passed to the container (rule 9 of docs/ecosystem/03 §2).

PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=production
LOG_LEVEL=info
CLOUDSFORGE_TAG=dev

# Rule 1: one database, named by this service's own variable. Note what is NOT here: a connection
# string for the ledger. Billing reaches the ledger over HTTP with a scoped token, never by
# connecting to its tables — AD-06.
BILLING_DATABASE_URL=postgres://cloudsforge:CHANGE_ME@postgres:5432/billing
BILLING_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# Token verification. `POST /purchases` and the revoke route accept a user (or an admin) and a
# service token carrying `billing:grant`; `GET /internal/entitlements/:userId` requires a service
# token carrying `billing:read` — the scope that finally lets a service ask whether a user owns
# something. The catalogue is public.
IDENTITY_JWKS_URL=http://identity:4000/.well-known/jwks.json
IDENTITY_ISSUER=https://identity.cloudsforge.online

# HMAC key for outbound event signatures. Run `openssl rand -base64 48`. The boot guard
# checks the SHAPE — base64 or hex, 32 decoded bytes, a measured entropy floor — so a typed
# value is refused however long it is, and there is no NODE_ENV exemption (micro-org #142).
OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_run_openssl_rand_base64_48

# The secrets POST /v1/events will ACCEPT, comma-separated, newest first. Optional: unset means
# "just OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET", which is the behaviour a deploy that ignores this line already has.
# It exists so the estate's shared key can be rotated one service at a time — a receiver that
# accepts only the outgoing key 403s every erasure event the instant identity's relay moves.
# EVERY ENTRY IS HELD TO THE SAME SHAPE AS THE SIGNING KEY. A rotation window that admits a
# placeholder "just for the drain" is how the leaked value survives the rotation meant to
# remove it, and the outgoing key is the one an attacker already has.
# OUTBOX_ACCEPT_SECRETS=CHANGE_ME_new_openssl_rand_base64_48,CHANGE_ME_old_openssl_rand_base64_48

# --- the ledger ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the ledger is. Every purchase, renewal and refund is a balanced journal entry posted here
# with an idempotency key. Billing holds no balance of its own.
BILLING_LEDGER_URL=http://ledger:4000

# The long-lived credential billing exchanges for the short-lived tokens it presents to its peers.
#
# THIS REPLACES BOTH BILLING_LEDGER_TOKEN AND BILLING_ADMIN_API_TOKEN, which were TOKENS — and a
# service token expires in 600 seconds (identity/src/tokens.ts:28). They were read once at boot and
# nothing re-minted them, so ten minutes into every deployment every posting to the ledger failed.
#
# ONE credential for both peers: identity reads the service off the credential row and never off
# the request, so one credential mints everything billing is allowed. The two clients still get
# SEPARATE, NARROW tokens — `ledger:*` and the exact `admin:read` — because the scope set is a
# request parameter, not a second secret. That keeps AD-05's separation and drops one long-lived
# bearer string.
#
# A credential does not expire, is revocable, and confers nothing by itself. The ten minutes is
# unchanged: rotation IS expiry (SD-12).
#
# `deploy/scripts/estate-bootstrap.sh` writes it to compose/estate/tokens.env. It begins `cfsc_`;
# if what you have begins `eyJ` it is a token, not a credential, and the service will refuse it.
#
# Technically optional — the image must be able to boot without one so CI can smoke-test /livez —
# but without it every call to a peer fails 503, and /readyz reports `identity-credential` as a
# hard failure so the replica takes no traffic.
BILLING_IDENTITY_CREDENTIAL=CHANGE_ME_TO_A_SERVICE_CREDENTIAL

# Where identity is, for the credential exchange. Defaults to IDENTITY_ISSUER, which is already
# required and is identity's own base URL. Only set this where the two genuinely differ.
# IDENTITY_URL=http://identity:4000

# Absolute wall-clock ceiling on a ledger call, across retries. It bounds how long a purchase
# transaction stays open, because the posting happens inside it — see the note in purchases.ts.
BILLING_LEDGER_DEADLINE_MS=5000

# How long an idempotency key is honoured. Expiring one EARLY means the next replay of it buys the
# thing a second time, so this must outlive every caller's retry horizon.
BILLING_IDEMPOTENCY_TTL_DAYS=30

# --- the engagement fee recycle (docs/ecosystem/21 §3) -------------------------------------------

# Where micro-admin-api is. UNSET IS A SUPPORTED MODE and means something true: this deployment
# runs no engagement programme, so no share of fee revenue is recycled into
# `platform:engagement-treasury`. The hourly job still finishes any period the ledger already owes
# an answer about; it closes no new ones.
#
# Note what is NOT here: a percentage. The rate lives in admin-api's `engagement_fee_recycle` row,
# starts at 0, and is raised only through the two-operator `engagement.policy.set` action. A copy
# of it in this service's environment would be a second thing to raise, bypassing that gate.
# ADMIN_API_URL=http://admin-api:4000

# There is no second token here any more. The admin-api client exchanges BILLING_IDENTITY_CREDENTIAL
# for a token narrowed to the EXACT scope `admin:read` — admin-api matches scopes exactly, so
# `admin:*` will not do.
#
# NOTE BEFORE ENABLING THIS. billing's entry in the estate's IDENTITY_SERVICE_TOKEN_GRANTS is
# ["ledger:read","ledger:post","ledger:reserve"] and does NOT include `admin:read`, so the exchange
# will fail with identity's ScopeNotGrantedError naming the missing scope. That is deliberate and
# is better than the 403 with no explanation the old static token produced. The fix is one entry in
# that grants map, in micro-deploy.

# Absolute wall-clock ceiling on the policy read, across retries.
# BILLING_ADMIN_API_DEADLINE_MS=5000

# Names this replica in jobs.locked_by. Defaults to the hostname, which is the container id under
# compose and the pod name under Kubernetes.
# INSTANCE_ID=

# Database tests run only against a database whose name contains "test", because they truncate.
# Unset, every database test skips.
# BILLING_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://cloudsforge:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/billing_test
